    "content": "Seychelles is a 115-island archipelago in the Indian Ocean off East Africa, known for its stunning,, white-sand beaches, UNESCO-listed nature reserves like Vallée de Mai, and luxurious, eco-friendly tourism. The nation, with a population of just over 100,000, offers a diverse Creole culture and acts as a year-round paradise with a tropical climate. Key Travel Information & Highlights Best Islands to Visit: Mahé (hub with capital Victoria), Praslin, and La Digue are the main inhabited islands, featuring famous spots like Anse Source D'Argent. Visa Requirements: Visitors must complete an online travel authorization form before arrival to avoid high fees. Best Time to Visit: April, May, October, and November are ideal for calmer, warmer weather suited for diving and sailing. Culture & Languages: A vibrant melting pot of African, French, and British influences, the official languages are Seychellois Creole, English, and French. Activities: Famous for island-hopping, snorkeling, scuba diving, visiting, and exploring, as well as bird-watching on Bird Island. Key Facts Official Language: Seychellois Creole, English, French. Population: Approx. 100,000+. Currency: Seychellois Rupee (SCR). Capital: Victoria. The islands are known for their high-end,, sustainable tourism, providing an exclusive and, intimate experience for visitors.",
